\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Sweet is the work, my God, my King,
\par To praise Thy name, give thanks, and 
\par sing;
\par To show Thy love by morning light,
\par And talk of all Thy truth at night.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Sweet is the day of sacred rest,
\par No mortal cares disturb my breast:
\par O may my heart in tune be found
\par Like David's harp of solemn sound!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. My heart shall triumph in the Lord,
\par And bless His works, and bless His 
\par word:
\par Thy works of grace, how bright
\par they shine!
\par How deep Thy counsels, how divine!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And I shall share a glorious part,
\par When grace has well refined my 
\par heart,
\par And fresh supplies of joy are shed,
\par Like holy oil to cheer my head.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then shall I see, and hear, and know
\par All I desired and wished below:
\par And every power find sweet employ
\par In that eternal world of joy.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

